    "sources": {
        "files": "Every sound file is mastered to -26 LUFS integrated, mono, true peak at most -1 dBTP; credits in the wiki's Sound-Credits page.",
        "levels": "Volumes set against vanilla by calculation from its code: in the game a sound plays at its file's loudness + 20 log10(volume x the player's setting for its type x distance attenuation). Distance attenuation is OpenAL exponent-clamped with reference max(3, sqrt(range) - 2) and rolloff ln 100 / ln range; weather and our beds play relative to the listener, unattenuated. Vanilla at sea: wind -39 LUFS just audible, -31 at wind speed 0.7, -24 in a full gale; rain -33 moderate, -27 heavy; raft idle -50; shore lapping -51 beside 100 edge blocks.",
        "beds": "Calm -48 LUFS, level with the raft idle and vanilla's shore lapping; moderate -36 and storm -29, 5 dB under vanilla's wind at the same sea.",
        "shore": "Block ambient, volume clamp(sqrt(blocks) / surfBlockCount) x strength. Surf -44 LUFS beside a gentle shore, -35 beside 400 breaking blocks in a 1.5 m sea, -28 on a storm coast. Lapping replaces vanilla's waterwaves (-36.75 LUFS) with a -26 LUFS file at 0.29 x the strength vanilla's would need.",
        "hull": "At a rider 1.5 m away: knock -40 light to -30 hard, break-up -28; slap -40 to -32, breaker slam -27, full bilge slosh -34, hull lapping -44. The whitecap hiss -37 LUFS at 12 m, under a force-6 wind."
